.TH RRRR 1 "September 2026" "rrrr 1.2.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rrrr \- Reliable Recursive Redundant RSync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rrrr
.RB [ \-hv ]
.I hostname
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBrrrr\fR orchestrates snapshot-style backups via \fBrsync\fR over SSH.
Each run pulls a fresh copy of a remote filesystem, reuses unchanged data with
\fB\-\-link\-dest\fR, updates a \fBlatest\fR symlink, and prunes snapshots based
on daily/weekly/monthly retention counts.
.PP
The tool is host-driven: the \fIhostname\fR argument selects a directory that
describes how to reach the remote server and where to store the snapshots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show help text.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the rrrr version.
.TP
.B \-V
Compatibility alias for \fB\-v\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The script inspects the following locations in order until it finds a matching
directory named after the specified hostname:
.IP "1." 4
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR/\fBrrrr\fR/\fIhostname\fR (default: \fB~/.config\fR)
.IP "2." 4
Each entry in \fB$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR (default: \fB/etc/xdg\fR), under
\fBrrrr\fR/\fIhostname\fR
.IP "3." 4
\fB/etc/rrrr\fR/\fIhostname\fR
.PP
Every host directory must provide a readable \fBconfig\fR file which is sourced
by the shell. Optionally, a \fBfilters\fR file may be present; when found it is
merged into rsync via \fB\-\-filter="merge <path>"\fR to fine-tune inclusion and
exclusion rules beyond the builtin defaults. If neither a host-local file nor a
\fBFILTERS_FILE\fR override is available, rrrr writes a temporary merge file
containing the typical runtime filesystem exclusions.
.SS Required variables
.TP
\fBREMOTE_USER\fR
SSH user that owns the remote data.
.TP
\fBSSH_KEY\fR
Private key on the backup host used to authenticate as \fBREMOTE_USER\fR.
.TP
\fBBACKUP_ROOT\fR
Local directory containing \fBsnapshots\fR, \fBlatest\fR, and \fBlogs\fR.
It may instead be set by an optional storage mount hook.
.SS Optional variables
.TP
\fBHOSTNAME_REMOTE\fR
Label used in logs. Defaults to the supplied hostname.
.TP
\fBREMOTE_SSH_HOST\fR, \fBREMOTE_SSH_PORT\fR
Actual address and optional port override for the remote SSH service. The
hostname defaults to the supplied hostname. When the port is unset, SSH
configuration (or SSH's own default) selects it.
.TP
\fBREMOTE_ROOT\fR
Remote path to sync (default: \fB/\fR).
.TP
\fBRSYNC_VERBOSE\fR
Rsync output level: \fB0\fR (default), \fB1\fR (\fB-v\fR), \fB2\fR
(\fB-vv\fR), or \fB3\fR (\fB-vvv\fR).
.TP
\fBRSYNC_PRESERVE_ACLS\fR
Preserve ACLs with \fB-A\fR (\fB1\fR, default) or disable it (\fB0\fR)
when source and destination ACL formats are incompatible.
.TP
\fBRSYNC_KEEP_PARTIAL\fR
Retain rsync exit-23 results under \fBpartials\fR (\fB1\fR) instead of
deleting the temporary snapshot (\fB0\fR, default). Retained partial snapshots
are never made \fBlatest\fR and rrrr keeps exit status 23.
.TP
\fBRSYNC_ACCEPT_PARTIAL\fR
Publish rsync exit-23 results as the current snapshot and update
\fBlatest\fR (\fB1\fR); disabled by default.
.TP
\fBKEEP_DAILY\fR, \fBKEEP_WEEKLY\fR, \fBKEEP_MONTHLY\fR
Retention counts (defaults: 7, 4, 6).
.TP
\fBFILTERS_FILE\fR
Path to a custom rsync filter file (used when a host-local \fBfilters\fR file is
not present).
.TP
\fBSNAPS_DIR\fR, \fBLOG_DIR\fR, \fBLATEST_LINK\fR
Override the default locations inside \fBBACKUP_ROOT\fR.
.SS Optional storage hooks
By default, rrrr writes directly to \fBBACKUP_ROOT\fR. A sourced config may
define both \fBrrrr_storage_mount\fR and \fBrrrr_storage_unmount\fR to mount
and release image files, encrypted volumes, datasets, or network storage.
The mount hook must set \fBBACKUP_ROOT\fR to an existing writable directory.
rrrr calls the mount hook before preparing backup paths and calls the unmount
hook whenever it exits, including after rsync fails or is interrupted. This
keeps the storage backend platform-specific while rrrr remains portable.
.SS Built-in APFS sparse bundle storage
On macOS, set \fBSTORAGE_PROVIDER=apfs-sparsebundle\fR to store a host's
snapshots in one APFS sparse bundle. Set \fBSTORAGE_IMAGE\fR to the sparse
bundle path. When it does not exist, \fBSTORAGE_IMAGE_SIZE\fR is required and
sets its maximum virtual capacity. The sparse bundle consumes host filesystem
space only as backup data is stored.
.PP
rrrr mounts the sparse bundle for the backup and detaches it when rrrr exits,
including after a failed run. \fBSTORAGE_MOUNTPOINT\fR is optional and defaults
to a private temporary directory. Set \fBSTORAGE_VOLUME_NAME\fR to change the
APFS volume label; it defaults to \fBrrrr-<hostname>\fR. The provider requires
macOS \fBhdiutil\fR and must not be combined with custom storage hooks.
.PP
For a Linux source backed up to macOS, set \fBRSYNC_PRESERVE_ACLS=0\fR because
Linux ACLs cannot be represented as macOS ACLs.
.PP
When unreadable paths are expected, set \fBRSYNC_ACCEPT_PARTIAL=1\fR to publish
exit-23 runs as the current snapshot. The skipped paths remain in the run log.
.PP
SSH inherits terminal input. When the key needs a passphrase or the remote host
requires a password, its prompt remains interactive. rrrr sends both rsync
output and errors to the terminal and run log.
.SS Built-in ext4 image storage
On Linux systems, set \fBSTORAGE_PROVIDER=ext4-image\fR to store a host's
snapshots in one ext4 filesystem image. Set \fBSTORAGE_IMAGE\fR to the image
file. When the image does not exist, \fBSTORAGE_IMAGE_SIZE_MIB\fR is required
and specifies its creation size in MiB. rrrr attaches the image to a loop
device for the backup and detaches it when rrrr exits.
.PP
\fBSTORAGE_MOUNTPOINT\fR is optional. When unset, rrrr creates and removes a
private temporary mountpoint. The provider requires permission to use
\fBlosetup\fR, \fBmount\fR, and \fBumount\fR, plus \fBmkfs.ext4\fR when
creating an image.
.PP
Set \fBSTORAGE_ELEVATE_USER\fR when these operations need a privileged QNAP
account. rrrr invokes only image lifecycle commands with
\fBsudo -n -u\fR and changes the mounted image root back to the backup user.
Configure a narrowly scoped passwordless sudo rule; rrrr never prompts for a
password. Images disable the \fBmetadata_csum_seed\fR ext4 feature for
compatibility with older QNAP kernels.
.SH OPERATION
The workflow is:
.IP "1." 4
Mount optional backup storage, validate required commands, and confirm the SSH
key/filter file exist.
.IP "2." 4
Create \fBsnapshots/YYYY\-MM\-DD\fR and compute a prior snapshot for
\fB\-\-link\-dest\fR when the \fBlatest\fR symlink points to a valid directory.
.IP "3." 4
Run \fBrsync -aHAX --numeric-ids --delete\fR with the configured filter file.
Output is mirrored to
\fBLOG_DIR\fR/\fBYYYY\-MM\-DD.log\fR.
.IP "4." 4
Publish the completed temporary snapshot, update \fBlatest\fR, and prune old
snapshots based on the retention policy. If rsync fails, the temporary
snapshot is removed and \fBlatest\fR is unchanged, so the backup can be
retried on the same day:
.PD 0
.RS
.IP \- 4
Keep the newest \fBKEEP_DAILY\fR snapshots.
.IP \- 4
Keep the newest \fBKEEP_WEEKLY\fR whose date is a Sunday.
.IP \- 4
Keep the newest \fBKEEP_MONTHLY\fR whose day is 01.
.RE
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rrrr\fR, \fB$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/rrrr\fR, \fB/etc/rrrr\fR
Host configuration directories.
.TP
\fBBACKUP_ROOT/snapshots\fR
Daily snapshot directories (\fBYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR).
.TP
\fBBACKUP_ROOT/latest\fR
Symlink to the most recent snapshot.
.TP
\fBBACKUP_ROOT/logs/YYYY\-MM\-DD.log\fR
Captured stdout/stderr for each run.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Primary location for per-user configuration (defaults to \fB~/.config\fR).
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\fR
Colon-separated list of additional configuration roots (defaults to
\fB/etc/xdg\fR).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
rrrr requires Bash 3 or newer, \fBrsync\fR, and OpenSSH. The built-in ext4
image provider additionally requires \fBlosetup\fR, \fBmount\fR,
\fBumount\fR, and \fBmkfs.ext4\fR when creating an image.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success. Exits non-zero if configuration is missing, the SSH
connection or rsync invocation fails, or retention processing encounters an
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrsync\fR(1), \fBssh\fR(1)
